{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792352304,"nonce":"0lk1BN4feHqJDDXGbOkJHfT39IA=","title":"Preview: lay out text and inline elements as one flow","message":"The Extension Studio's Preview places each text node and each inline element (`strong`, `em`, `code`, `a`) as a box of its own, so `\u003cp\u003ea \u003cstrong\u003eb\u003c/strong\u003e c\u003c/p\u003e` drops the spaces at the edge of each box and does not wrap as a paragraph.\n\nashui lays such content out with `ashui.text.InlineFlow`, which its HXX macro attaches to `p`, `h1`–`h6`, `dt`, `dd`, `caption`, `legend` and `figcaption`. The Preview builds nodes with `tree.createNode()`, so it never attaches one.\n\nWhat blocks attaching a flow: `InlineFlow.attach` takes a `Div` and registers `Owner.onCleanup`, so it needs an owner scope that outlives the Preview's `show()`/`hide()` cycle; and it inserts its own anchor and spacer nodes among the root's children, which the Preview's `replaceChildren` placement would remove.\n\nThe Markdown fixture (tests/fixtures/markdown) works around it by emitting each word as a flex-wrap item with the following space kept as a no-break space on the word. Remove that once the Preview flows text.","files":null}]}